   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Standard operating procedures developed for teams for crime scene investigation, documenting the crime scene, taking and packaging evidence for explosives and teams trained to use SOPs
SOP on developed in line with international standards, taking into account local experience and domestic legislation
Officers acquired knowledge through series of trainings

2. The capacity of Arson and Explosives Laboratory increased
SOPs for the Arson and Explosives Laboratory developed in line with international standards
Necessary equipment for the laboratory acquired
Professionals working in the Arson and Explosives Laboratory acquired knowledge through series of trainings on developed SOPs
Work processes accredited, making them recognized and valid internationally, thus enabling the efficient exchange and international cooperation in fight against crime

3. The capacities of the chemical laboratory increased
SOPs for the Chemical Laboratory developed in line with international standards
Necessary equipment for the laboratory acquired
Professionals working in the Chemical Laboratory acquired knowledge through series of trainings on developed SOPs
Work processes accredited, making them recognized and valid internationally, thus enabling the efficient exchange and international cooperation in fight against crime</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Standard operating procedures developed for teams for crime scene investigation, documenting the crime scene, taking and packaging evidence for explosives and teams trained to use SOPs
No SOPs on explosives in place
Professionals not trained on SOPs on explosives

2. The capacity of Arson and Explosives Laboratory increased
No SOPs in place
No adequate equipment
Methods not accredited

3. The capacities of the chemical laboratory increased
No SOPs in place
No adequate equipment
Methods for explosives not accredited</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Standard operating procedures developed for teams for crime scene investigation, documenting the crime scene, taking and packaging evidence for explosives and teams trained to use SOPs
Standard operating procedures developed

2. The capacity of Arson and Explosives Laboratory increased
Standard operating procedures for increasing security and ensuring accreditation and standardization of the methods of work developed
Capacity of A&amp;E laboratory upgraded with technical equipment 

3. The capacities of the chemical laboratory increased
Standard operating procedures developed
Teams from chemical lab trained</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gap analyses finalised. Purchasing sophisticated equipment contracted and delivery expected in the beginning of next year. Standard Operating Procedures for Crime Scene Investigation (CSI) unit for packaging and tagging of evidence, and chain of custody applicable to all CSI units in Montenegro and procedures in the area of CSI applicable to explosions drafted.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The capacity of Crime Scene Investigation Unit, Arson and Explosives and Chemical Laboratory increased by reviewing Standard operating procedures for increasing security and support preparations for accreditation and standardization of the methods of work in both labs. Capacity of Crime Scene Investigation Unit, Chemical and A&amp;E laboratory upgraded with technical equipment</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Capacity of the Forensic Center - Crime Scene investigation Unit, Arson and Explosive Lab and Chemical Lab increased through development and revision of standard operating procedures, procurement of highly specialised equipment and training of professionals to use the equipment and SOPs developed.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
